---
title: "Brand Preview — Penumbra Forge"
description: "Concept preview for a stronger Penumbra Forge brand direction."
permalink: /preview/brand/
---
{% extends "base.njk" %}

{% block headExtra %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow">
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="brand-preview-page">
  <div class="brand-preview-banner">
    <a href="/">← Back to current site</a>
    <span>Concept preview for approval</span>
  </div>

  <main class="brand-preview-shell">
    <section class="brand-review-intro">
      <p class="brand-review-kicker">Refined Directions</p>
      <h1>Two stronger identities for a founder-led, serious Penumbra Forge.</h1>
      <p class="brand-review-lead">You said you want the brand to feel professional, founder-led, and operator-grade. So this round moves away from abstract icon hunting and into two fuller identity systems that could actually anchor the site.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="brand-direction-grid" id="brand-directions">
      <article class="brand-direction-card brand-direction-card--founder">
        <div class="brand-direction-header">
          <div>
            <p class="brand-review-kicker">Direction A</p>
            <h2>Founder Signature</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="brand-direction-note">Best for trust, authorship, and premium clarity.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="brand-lockup brand-lockup--founder">
          <img src="/branding/penumbra-mark-founder-signature.svg" alt="Founder Signature mark">
          <div>
            <p class="brand-lockup-word brand-lockup-word--founder">Penumbra Forge</p>
            <p class="brand-lockup-sub">By Shadoe Myers</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="brand-home-sample brand-home-sample--founder">
          <p class="brand-home-eyebrow">Independent software studio</p>
          <h3>Privacy-first security tools and local AI, built by Shadoe Myers.</h3>
          <p>A more personal, founder-forward approach that says this is a real studio run by a real operator with domain credibility, not an anonymous side project.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="brand-application-grid">
          <div class="brand-application-card">
            <p class="brand-application-label">Header</p>
            <div class="brand-mini-header brand-mini-header--founder">
              <span>Penumbra Forge</span>
              <span>By Shadoe Myers</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="brand-application-card">
            <p class="brand-application-label">Social card tone</p>
            <div class="brand-mini-social">
              <p class="brand-mini-social-title">Independent software, forged by experience.</p>
              <p>Security tools, local AI, and automation from a founder with real operator background.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="brand-application-card">
            <p class="brand-application-label">Icon / favicon</p>
            <div class="brand-mini-mark">
              <img src="/branding/penumbra-mark-founder-signature.svg" alt="">
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <ul class="brand-direction-points">
          <li>Your name becomes an asset instead of a footnote.</li>
          <li>The site feels more premium and established immediately.</li>
          <li>Penumbra stays central without needing a loud icon.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="brand-direction-card brand-direction-card--operator">
        <div class="brand-direction-header">
          <div>
            <p class="brand-review-kicker">Direction B</p>
            <h2>Operator Grade</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="brand-direction-note">Best for authority, precision, and business seriousness.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="brand-lockup brand-lockup--operator">
          <img src="/branding/penumbra-mark-operator-grade.svg" alt="Operator Grade mark">
          <div>
            <p class="brand-lockup-word brand-lockup-word--operator">PENUMBRA FORGE</p>
            <p class="brand-lockup-sub brand-lockup-sub--operator">Security tools / Local AI / Automation</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="brand-home-sample brand-home-sample--operator">
          <p class="brand-home-eyebrow">Operator-grade software</p>
          <h3>Security tooling, local AI, and automation for people who take their stack seriously.</h3>
          <p>A more technical and corporate-credible system that makes the business feel sharper, more disciplined, and more mature at first glance.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="brand-application-grid">
          <div class="brand-application-card">
            <p class="brand-application-label">Header</p>
            <div class="brand-mini-header brand-mini-header--operator">
              <span>PENUMBRA FORGE</span>
              <span>Studio / Tools / GitHub</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="brand-application-card">
            <p class="brand-application-label">Social card tone</p>
            <div class="brand-mini-social brand-mini-social--operator">
              <p class="brand-mini-social-title">Operator-grade software for privacy-first teams.</p>
              <p>Built by Shadoe Myers. Serious tools, local execution, minimal attack surface.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="brand-application-card">
            <p class="brand-application-label">Icon / favicon</p>
            <div class="brand-mini-mark">
              <img src="/branding/penumbra-mark-operator-grade.svg" alt="">
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <ul class="brand-direction-points">
          <li>The business reads more established and technical right away.</li>
          <li>It supports a stronger product family system over time.</li>
          <li>It can make the studio feel larger than one person, if overdone.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="brand-recommendation">
      <div class="brand-recommendation-main">
        <p class="brand-review-kicker">Recommended Blend</p>
        <h2>Founder-signature brand, operator-grade site.</h2>
        <p>The strongest answer may be combining both: make the logo and narrative feel founder-led and personal, then let the homepage structure, navigation, product pages, and copy system feel disciplined and operator-grade. That gives you authority without losing your identity.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="brand-recommendation-grid">
        <article class="brand-recommendation-card">
          <p class="brand-application-label">Logo</p>
          <p>Founder Signature</p>
        </article>
        <article class="brand-recommendation-card">
          <p class="brand-application-label">Homepage system</p>
          <p>Operator Grade</p>
        </article>
        <article class="brand-recommendation-card">
          <p class="brand-application-label">Voice</p>
          <p>Personal, credible, no fluff</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <div class="grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
